# The ledger of `image/text`: what Go's `golang.org/x/image/font` and
# `font/opentype` (`Drawer`, `DrawString`, `MeasureString`), Python's Pillow
# (`ImageFont`, `ImageDraw.text`, `textbbox`, `textlength`, `multiline_text`)
# and Java's `java.awt.font` (`TextLayout`, `GlyphVector`) let a program do to
# draw text into an image, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers.
# Go's x/image is not part of Go's standard library and is not on this machine,
# Pillow is not installed and Java's names are those of its documentation: their
# lines are the names the catalogue gives, unread by `go doc`, `dir()` or
# `javap`, a question rather than a measurement. Rust's standard library has
# no text drawing: `-` in its lines.
#
# No second rasteriser is on this machine to give the pixels of a glyph, so the
# tests hold what the definitions give: the ink of a letter has the area its
# outline encloses (the shoelace sum over the outline, computed in the test
# apart from the rasteriser), stands on the baseline row and spans the glyph's
# own box scaled to the size, a line drawn in two pieces ends as one drawn
# whole, and the same outline filled apart gives the same pixels. The font is
# Noto Sans Regular 2.015 cut to 29 glyphs (SIL Open Font License 1.1).

capability text/measure  the room a line takes: its width and the heights above and below its baseline
  heroes  image/text.measure, image/text.Measure
  go      font.MeasureString, font.Drawer.MeasureString, Face.Metrics, Face.GlyphAdvance
  rust    -
  python  ImageFont.getlength, ImageFont.getbbox, ImageFont.getmetrics, ImageDraw.textlength, ImageDraw.textbbox
  note    the width is the advances of the glyphs, the kerning of the `kern` table where asked and the spacing between letters; the heights are the font's ascent and descent at the size

capability text/draw  a line filled into an image
  heroes  image/text.draw, image/text.style, image/text.Style
  go      font.Drawer.DrawString, font.Drawer.Dot, opentype.NewFace
  rust    -
  python  ImageDraw.text
  note    the baseline row and the pen's column are given, the glyphs anti-aliased by their alpha over what is there and cut by the image's edge; the answer is how far the pen travelled, where Go's Drawer moves its own `Dot`

capability text/outline  the outline of a line as a path
  heroes  image/text.outline
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  ImageFont.getmask2, ImageFont.FreeTypeFont.font.render
  note    the path is `image/vector`'s, so a program strokes it (a Pillow `stroke_width`), turns it, scales it or fills it with a rule of its own

capability text/block  text cut into lines and aligned in a width
  heroes  image/text.wrap, image/text.draw_block, image/text.Align
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  ImageDraw.multiline_text, ImageDraw.multiline_textbbox, ImageDraw.text (align, spacing)
  note    paragraphs at line feeds, words at spaces, a word wider than the line cut between characters, left, centre and right alignment and a factor on the font's line height

capability text/missing  a character the font cannot show
  heroes  image/text.Style: notdef
  go      font.Face.GlyphAdvance (not ok)
  rust    -
  python  ImageFont.getmask (the notdef box)
  note    `not_found` naming the character, before a pixel changes, or the font's own `.notdef` where the style asks for it

capability text/shaping  complex-script shaping and right-to-left text
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  ImageFont.Layout.RAQM, ImageDraw.text (direction, features, language)
  note    the order of right-to-left text, the joined forms of Arabic, ligatures and GPOS pair adjustments (see `font/layout`) wait for a shaper; Latin, Greek and Cyrillic set left to right are complete

capability text/hinting  glyphs fitted to the pixel grid, and the sub-pixel positions of LCD text
  heroes  refused: the outlines are filled as the font draws them at its size, which is what Go's `font.HintingNone` and a plotter want; a rasteriser that runs the font's instructions is `font/hinting`'s refusal
  go      font.HintingNone, font.HintingVertical, font.HintingFull
  rust    -
  python  ImageFont.Layout, FreeTypeFont (layout_engine)
  note    -

dropped
  go      font.Face as an interface and its Close: a font is a value here, parsed by `font.parse`
  python  ImageFont.load_default, ImageFont.truetype by path or by name: the bytes and the system's fonts are `font`'s; ImageFont.TransposedFont: turn the image after drawing
